  "narrative": "The first discovery round provides no support for any registered positive-direction hypothesis as written. Because returned estimates are already signed to the hypothesis direction, a positive estimate supports the claimed direction and a negative estimate opposes it. I used an approximate absolute-mean-difference benchmark for clinical relevance: about 10% of the population absolute outcome mean. For most outcome_013-like outcomes with mean around -0.25 to -0.27, this corresponds to roughly 0.025-0.027; for outcome_006 and outcome_014, whose means are closer to zero, the absolute threshold is smaller, around 0.009. This is an interpretation convention rather than an exact scale-preserving relative calculation, but it is conservative because the outcomes are mostly negative dependency scores. H1, H9, and H12 are rejected because even the upper 95% interval for the hypothesized positive association is small relative to the relevant outcome scale. H2 and H4 are rejected as positive claims because their intervals do not meaningfully support a clinically relevant positive interaction or positive main effect; however, H4 shows a large opposite-point main effect on outcome_006, so I registered a refinement in the opposite direction for later follow-up rather than validating it now. H3 and H10 are interactions or small-mean comparisons where the intervals remain wide enough to include both null and clinically meaningful values in the hypothesized direction, so I left them unresolved but deferred. H5, H6, and H11 are also unresolved and deferred: each has point estimates below approximate clinical thresholds or small exposed cells, especially H11 with only 76 exposed observations. The strongest result is H7. Its signed estimate is negative despite claiming a positive association, so the original H7 claim is rejected. The same evidence indicates the opposite raw association: among feature_043-high eligible samples, feature_065=1 has a mean outcome_013 difference of about -0.095 versus feature_065=0, meaning stronger dependency, with a 95% interval of roughly -0.167 to -0.024. The estimate is clearly above the approximate 10% threshold, although the least extreme confidence-boundary value is near the threshold. Because this is one of twelve unadjusted discovery tests, I do not accept the opposite claim yet, but the association is promising enough to request independent validation of H7's comparison. I also registered a refinement with direction -1 so that, if validation is favorable, the scientifically meaningful association can be assessed as an opposite-direction claim rather than misrepresenting the original positive hypothesis. I did not validate H4 yet because its interval crosses zero and its exposed group is only moderately sized, despite the large point estimate; validation capacity should focus first on H7. The cell sizes are all valid under the analysis rule, but small or restricted subgroups remain vulnerable to random noise and unmeasured confounding. These are associations in this supplied dataset only, not causal claims or claims about generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Round 1 result summary. Most original positive claims are unsupported or negligible. Approximate clinical thresholds: outcome_013 ~0.027; outcome_001 ~0.042; outcome_008 ~0.028; outcome_011 ~0.030; outcome_012/005/015/002/016/007/004/009/010/003 ~0.025; outcome_014 and outcome_006 ~0.009. Key candidate: H7/refinement to opposite direction: in feature_043>=8.37875, feature_065=1 vs 0 gives outcome_013 approximately -0.095 (stronger dependency), CI -0.167 to -0.024. Original positive H7 rejected; active for validation and refinement. Secondary candidate: H4/refinement opposite direction: outcome_006 feature_045=1 vs 0 point approximately -0.031, CI -0.067 to +0.004; not robust yet. Deferred unresolved: H3, H5, H6, H10, H11. H11 small exposed cell (76). Closed rejects: H1, H2, H8, H9, H12. Multiplicity caution: 12 discovery tests; H7 opposite needs validation. Remaining outcomes outcome_002, outcome_004, outcome_007, outcome_016 still need exploration. Future plan: assess H7 validation; if robust, accept opposite refinement; otherwise close or keep unresolved. Consider follow-up for H4 opposite only if validation resources remain and after broader outcome coverage. Avoid causal interpretation due to opaque predictors and possible confounding.",
  "validate": "H7"
