  "research_notes": "Updated after appraise round 2. Accepted H28 and H29: outcome_013 feature_065=1 vs 0 under feature_043>=5.256 and unrestricted, direction -1. Raw differences are negative, signed estimates ~+0.116 with lower bounds ~+0.065 and ~+0.082, respectively, clearly above the approximate outcome_013 clinical threshold (~0.027). This broadens the dataset-internal scope of the earlier accepted H13 from feature_043-high to upper-half and unrestricted eligibility, within this dataset only. Rejected/closed H27 interaction: negative interaction not supported; interval wide and point opposite. Broad screens H15/H17/H19/H21 rejected as clinically negligible for registered directions; H20 rejected because it is opposite/small. H16/H18/H23 deferred unresolved because point estimates are weak despite some intervals including clinically relevant values. H22 is the main active new signal: outcome_016 feature_065=1 vs 0 under feature_043>=8.37875, signed estimate ~+0.055, discovery CI ~[+0.015,+0.094]; lower CI is below the approximate clinical threshold (~0.026), so validation requested. Registered refinements H34-H36 to test outcome_016 feature_065 unrestricted, upper-half eligibility, and high-vs-complement interaction. Next analyze candidates: H24/H25/H26/H30-H33 (outcome_012/014/015/005/009/010/011 feature_065 in feature_043-high) plus H34-H36 if H22-related follow-up is desired. H14 remains active unresolved: outcome_006 feature_045 opposite direction, signed estimate ~+0.031 with lower CI just below zero; not validated now because H22 was the more direct cross-outcome replication of an accepted marker. Keep causal and mechanistic interpretation open; predictor labels remain opaque. Approximate clinical thresholds used: outcome_001 ~0.042, outcome_002 ~0.026, outcome_004 ~0.026, outcome_007 ~0.0245, outcome_013 ~0.027, outcome_016 ~0.0256, outcome_011 ~0.030, outcome_008 ~0.028, outcomes 003/005/009/010/012/015 ~0.025, outcome_006/014 ~0.009."
