evels (H68, H69). H13 was independently validated with R13 +0.1290 [0.0418, 0.2163], and H69 received independent validation with R103 +0.0998 [0.0331, 0.1666], both supporting the same signed direction. The association also holds in feature_045 strata (H60 +0.1676, H65 +0.1007), feature_027=0 (H79 +0.1269), feature_054 levels (H106 +0.1242, H107 +0.1144), feature_057 levels (H113 +0.1138, H114 +0.1220), and quartile or median extremes of feature_061 and feature_066 (H173 +0.1810, H175 +0.1118, H176 +0.1088; H147 +0.1547, H148 +0.0734, H150 +0.1405, H151 +0.0923). H148 should be treated as confirmatory persistence rather than a strong clinically significant stratum estimate because its lower bound is slightly below the operational 10% benchmark. The best conclusion is robustness of a broad feature_065-outcome_013 association within this dataset.\n\nEffect modification of the feature_065-outcome_013 association is generally not supported. Interactions around feature_043 (H27, H39), feature_034 (H52), and feature_045 (H58) did not support meaningful context dependence; H58 was rejected after inconsistent validation. High feature_010 modification (H153) and median feature_066 modification (H152) were also rejected. The high feature_061 interaction (H149) remains unresolved because the lower bound is near zero and far below the clinical benchmark; I closed it as an unproductive tested uncertainty. The evidence supports an internal robust marker-outcome association, not evidence that one covariate meaningfully amplifies or attenuates it.\n\nThe second major supported finding is feature_027=1 versus feature_027=0 associated with dramatically weaker outcome_014 dependency. H82 discovery is +0.7961 [0.7759, 0.8163], and independent validation R116 is +0.8005 [0.7721, 0.8290]. Accepted strata include H91-H94, H99, H100, H102-H105, H115, H116, H179, and H180, many with intervals near 0.77-0.85. The magnitude is far beyond ordinary dependency-score movement and many times the outcome_014 mean-scale benchmark. The scientifically responsible conclusion is a reproducible dataset-internal coding, surrogate, or leakage-like signal rather than ordinary biological dependency modulation. H154 showed no clinically meaningful modification of this weak-dependency association by positive feature_010 (interaction -0.0149 [-0.0556, 0.0258]).\n\nNegative or unsupported findings are substantial. Feature_065 does not have clinically meaningful interval-supported effects on many other dependency outcomes in the available tests: outcome_006 overall and refined feature_045 tests were rejected after validation or discovery (H4, H14, H43); outcome_011 overall (H128) was rejected; outcome_016 high feature_043 (H22) was not supported after validation; validated feature_015 in feature_045=0 (H70) was near null; high feature_043 strata for outcome_002, outcome_004, and outcome_014 were null or inconsistent after validation (H16, H18, H25). New feature_064 and feature_020 screens (H155, H157, H158) did not support clinically meaningful associations with outcome_013 or outcome_014. H156 remains unresolved but is weak evidence because feature_064 appears to duplicate feature_047 in the ledger and its interval crosses zero and the threshold.\n\nFeature_027 does not show a broad clinically meaningful effect outside outcome_014. Many outcome-specific contrasts were rejected or remained borderline unresolved, including outcome_015 (H83), outcome_012 (H84), outcome_008 (H85), outcome_011 (H86), outcome_016 (H122), outcome_002 (H135), outcome_003 (H140), and several small outcome_013 contrasts. The conditional feature_027 outcome_013 effect in feature_045=1 (H76) was rejected after validation, and the conditional feature_065 effect in feature_045=0 with feature_027=1 (H126) was validated but inconclusive: discovery +0.0616 [-0.0227, 0.1459], validation +0.1236 [-0.0279, 0.2752]. This small conditional subgroup cannot be used to claim context-dependent biology.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty centers on borderline overall or stratum feature_065 effects, small conditional contexts, and untested outcome specificity. Overall feature_065 effects remain unresolved for outcome_012 (H73 +0.0169 [-0.0027, 0.0365]), outcome_015 (H62 +0.0211 [0.0018, 0.0404]), outcome_005 (H61 +0.0155 [-0.0037, 0.0348]), outcome_014 (H95 +0.0319 [-0.0074, 0.0711]), and outcome_001 (H63 +0.0089 [-0.0319, 0.0496]). The low feature_061 stratum (H174) remains unresolved but closed. Feature_024 quartile feature_065 tests are borderline or unresolved. Feature_057 dose contrasts are unresolved or rejected. Feature_064/feature_047 duplicate-screen evidence is not decisive. Because outcome specificity claims H159-H166 are active and untested, we cannot say feature_065 has no effect on outcome_002, outcome_003, outcome_004, outcome_006, outcome_007, outcome_008, outcome_009, or outcome_010 beyond the specific tests already completed.\n\nThe most informative next analyses are internal outcome-specificity and context-robustness tests, not further validation. First, analyze H159-H166 to determine whether the broad feature_065 association is specific to outcome_013 or extends to other dependency outcomes. Second, analyze H167-H168 to confirm that the enormous feature_027-outcome_014 weak-dependency signal is stable across feature_061 and feature_066 contexts, even though current interactions suggest it is not meaningfully modified. Third, analyze H181-H183 and H184-H186 to test joint feature_061/feature_066, feature_056, upper feature_010, and feature_059 contexts for feature_065-outcome_013 effect modification. Fourth, analyze H187-H192 as independent categorical/binary predictor screens. All conclusions remain associations in this supplied dataset only. No causal mechanism, biological identity of opaque predictors, or external generalizability is established.",
