r bound falls just below the outcome_014 benchmark of 0.0093. Because the lower bound is below zero relative to the clinical rule, I do not accept it; I keep it unresolved but closed to indicate that it is not promotable without external or prespecified replication. H244/R243, in the feature_043<=5.256 complement, is not clinically established (point +0.0484; interval -0.0375, +0.1343), with lower bound below zero and benchmark; I reject that specific stratum-level claim. H245/R244, the feature_043 interaction, is imprecise and inconsistent with a clear enhancement (+0.0285; -0.0812, +0.1381), so I reject it as a localization test. H211 remains unresolved overall because its original lower bound narrowly cleared the benchmark, but it is closed because the prespecified localization battery failed to make it coherent or clinically accepted.\n\nThe modifier tests for the core feature_065--outcome_013 association do not yield a new accepted effect modifier. H183/R245 tests joint high feature_061 and feature_066; the interaction is positive (+0.1186) and has lower bound +0.0085, but this is statistically borderline and far below the outcome_013 benchmark. I keep it unresolved but closed rather than accept it. H184/R246, H185/R247, and H186/R248 are rejected: their positive interaction intervals include zero or estimates are negative, and lower bounds are below the outcome_013 benchmark. This supports the earlier conclusion that the accepted feature_065--outcome_013 association is broad and not reliably modified by the tested continuous or categorical strata, while not establishing mechanism or external generalizability.\n\nThe artifact-like feature_027--outcome_014 pattern remains best interpreted as data-structure, coding, provenance, or leakage-like, not biology. H167/R249 and H168/R250 test whether the enormous feature_027-outcome_014 contrast is modified by feature_061 and feature_066 age/body-like strata. Both interactions are near null and statistically inconclusiv