e repeated subgroup exploration and the instability across independent validation, H76 is downgraded to unresolved and closed. It is not used as part of the supported evidence.\n\nNegative and specificity findings. Feature_065 did not show a comparably meaningful association with the other 15 dependency outcomes. Overall or targeted clean-population tests for outcome_001 through outcome_012 and outcome_014 through outcome_016 were rejected, unresolved with intervals not clearing the benchmark, or centered near zero. Examples in clean feature_027=0 and feature_006=0 contexts include outcome_012 R262 +0.0169 [-0.0057, 0.0394], outcome_014 R255 +0.0153 [-0.0079, 0.0385], outcome_015 R256 +0.0193 [-0.0032, 0.0418], and outcome_016 R263 +0.0140 [-0.0095, 0.0376]; none clears its outcome-specific benchmark. Broad predictor screens involving feature_034, feature_002, feature_060, feature_042, feature_020, feature_063, feature_048, feature_011, feature_055, feature_019, feature_036, and other sparse binary features mostly yielded rejected or small intervals centered near zero. The final newly completed internal tests also did not support new clinically meaningful claims: H36 tested a feature_065-by-feature_043>=8.37875 interaction on outcome_016 and gave R268 -0.0556 [-0.1013, -0.0099], opposite the registered direction; H198 tested feature_035=1 versus 0 on outcome_014 and gave R269 -0.0439 [-0.0958, 0.0080], below the outcome_014 benchmark in the registered direction. Effect-modification searches did not produce a clinically meaningful interaction for feature_065 after accounting for benchmark, multiplicity, and validation status.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty. Some leads remain hypothesis-generating only. Feature_006=1 with outcome_014 has a direction -1 signed estimate of R199 +0.0647 [0.0108, 0.1186], which nominally clears the low outcome_014 benchmark but was discovered post hoc, involves sparse cells, is potentially entangled with the feature_027/outcome_014 artifact structure, and lacks a clean replicated localization. It remains unresolved and should not be biologically interpreted before data-integrity checks. Feature_065 has some statistically non-null but clinically below-benchmark signals for outcome_012 R157 +0.0215 [0.0001, 0.0429] and outcome_015 R62 +0.0211 [0.0018, 0.0404], and an imprecise unresolved signal for outcome_014 R98 +0.0319 [-0.0074, 0.0711]. Outcome_016 feature_045=1, feature_027=0, feature_006=0 contrasts are suggestive but lower bounds do not clear the outcome_016 benchmark after extensive subgroup exploration. Interaction estimates such as H183 R245 +0.1186 [0.0085, 0.2286] and H263 R267 +0.0999 [-0.0099, 0.2096] may be biologically interesting but are not supported as clinically meaningful effect modification because the lower bounds do not clear the outcome_013 benchmark and the searches were exploratory. Sparse cells remain unresolved because of uncertainty, not because they demonstrate true effect or true null.\n\nMost informative next analyses. First, externally preregister the feature_065=1 marker of stronger outcome_013 dependency. The replication should fix the primary comparison, eligibility definitions, outcome_013 benchmark, expected direction, adjustment for correlated predictors, handling of feature_027 and feature_006, and multiplicity or false-discovery control. Second, perform a provenance and leakage audit for feature_027 and outcome_014, and also for feature_006 and outcome_014 if that association remains of interest. Inspect variable derivation, generation logs, sample identifiers, duplicate rows, batch or cell-line structure, missingness patterns, and whether feature_027 or feature_006 are structurally coupled to outcome_014. If an artifact is found, exclude, recode, or stratify before any biological modeling. Third, do not allocate remaining effort to additional internal subgroup mining in this dataset; it is more likely to increase multiplicity than to change the conclusions. The most valuable remaining science is external validation of feature_065 for outcome_013 and a data-integrity audit of the extremely large feature_027-outcome_014 pattern.",
  "research_notes": "Final run status. Validation budget exhausted; no new validation or response deadlines. Reassessed H76 from accept to unresolved closed because discovery lower bound barely cleared the outcome_013 benchmark but independent validation failed to replicate clinically meaningful magnitude. Main accepted dataset-internal conclusion remains feature_065=1 associated with stronger outcome_013 dependency: overall +0.1169 [0.0823, 0.1516], with validated strata and robustness checks including clean feature_027=0 and feature_006=0 contexts. Secondary measured signal feature_027=1 with much weaker outcome_014 dependency is far too large to treat as ordinary biology; it is a data-structure/coding/leakage audit signal. Final internal tests H36 and H198 are rejected. No clinically meaningful feature_065 effect modifiers or comparable associations with other outcomes were accepted. Unresolved hypothesis-generating leads include feature_006 with outcome_014 and sparse or borderline interactions, all requiring external or integrity-focused follow-up. Next steps: preregistered external replication of feature_065-outcome_013 and provenance/leakage audit of feature_027/outcome_014; no further internal subgroup mining."
